  "term": "emotional memory",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, emotional memory refers to a recollection of the past in which the parts of an experience hold a fairly equal interest because they are all felt as belonging to one’s past. James contrasts it with more usual remembering, where only certain especially interesting details stand out above the rest.",
